---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Use – ispdf';
const description =
  'Terms for using the free ispdf tool to change PDF page size in your browser.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <main id="main" class="copy legal">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="legal-meta">Effective date: 21 October 2026</p>
    <p>
      These terms cover your use of ispdf at <a href="https://ispdf.org/">ispdf.org</a>. The site gives you a free way
      to change PDF page dimensions in your browser. By using it, you agree to these terms and to the
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>The tool</h2>
    <p>
      ispdf resizes PDF pages to a paper size or custom dimensions you choose. It does not compress a file to a target
      size in kilobytes or megabytes, and it does not require an account. Processing happens in your browser. Output
      depends on the PDF. Some damaged, encrypted, or unusually complex files cannot be resized, and the tool will say
      so instead of pretending the result is ready.
    </p>

    <h2>Your files</h2>
    <p>
      You are responsible for the PDFs you open in the tool. Use only files you have the right to modify. ispdf does
      not receive the file contents and does not check whether you may use a document. Keep your own copy. A resized
      download is created on your device and is not stored for you on our side.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not misuse the site. That includes attempting to break, overload, or probe the service, or using it in
      connection with unlawful activity. We may change, suspend, or remove the tool if that is needed to operate or
      protect the site.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The tool is provided as is and as available. We do not guarantee that every PDF will resize, that the result will
      meet a printer’s or institution’s rules, or that the site will be uninterrupted or error-free. Check the
      downloaded file before you rely on it.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, ispdf is not liable for lost files, lost profits, or other indirect damages
      arising from use of the site. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot legally be limited, including
      rights you have as a consumer where you live.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms or the tool. The current terms will be posted on this page with an effective date. If
      you keep using the site after a change, the updated terms apply to later use.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms can be sent to
      <a href="mailto:contact@ispdf.org">contact@ispdf.org</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
